  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes, especially when sentiment is negative or neutral.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward if sentiment history shows persistent negative sentiment (e.g., -0.20 or -0.25) over recent days.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-10% for next period.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment shifts from positive to negative (e.g., 0.00 → -0.20 or -0.25).",
    "Avoid overreacting to short-term volatility: if true outcome deviates >10% from forecast, apply smoothing filter (e.g., 3-day moving average) before next forecast.",
    "For horizon >15 days, reduce forecast volatility if sentiment remains flat or negative; use sentiment as a decay-weighted filter for long-term bias correction."
  ]
}
